1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,240
Beyond Marks explores the reasoning behind an answer.

2
00:00:03,240 --> 00:00:09,536
This is a walkthrough of the real application using demonstration activity, not classroom outcome data.

3
00:00:09,936 --> 00:00:16,265
The learner questions a flawed explanation, selects the faulty segment, and explains their thinking.

4
00:00:16,265 --> 00:00:20,316
Confidence and context are optional, and remain learner reports.

5
00:00:20,716 --> 00:00:27,525
Conceptual difficulty, misreading, time pressure, and unfinished work remain competing explanations.

6
00:00:27,525 --> 00:00:30,930
Evidence weights are not probabilities of ability.

7
00:00:30,930 --> 00:00:32,632
The learner can disagree.

8
00:00:33,032 --> 00:00:36,717
A report of time pressure leads to a fresh, unhurried probe.

9
00:00:36,717 --> 00:00:43,411
Distinct questions test different possibilities, while acknowledging when one answer cannot distinguish them.

10
00:00:43,811 --> 00:00:47,947
A short explanation and worked example lead to an active prediction.

11
00:00:47,947 --> 00:00:50,927
Opening a lesson does not count as completing it.

12
00:00:51,327 --> 00:00:55,336
The transfer challenge asks the learner to repair code in a new setting.

13
00:00:55,336 --> 00:00:58,398
The answer and selected reasoning are checked together.

14
00:00:58,798 --> 00:01:03,192
Independent verification removes earlier hints and asks for two results.

15
00:01:03,192 --> 00:01:07,708
A failed check returns to fresh support and a different verification task.

16
00:01:08,108 --> 00:01:11,500
Reflection asks for a counterexample and a better rule.

17
00:01:11,500 --> 00:01:15,940
Learners can pause, resume, or ask their teacher to review the evidence.

18
00:01:16,340 --> 00:01:20,926
Successful reflection schedules fresh checks after seven and thirty days.

19
00:01:20,926 --> 00:01:23,564
These checks are scheduled, not completed.

20
00:01:23,564 --> 00:01:27,522
Retained understanding can only be tested after the real delay.

21
00:01:27,922 --> 00:01:33,659
The teacher timeline keeps responses, interpretations, disagreement, and learner context visible.

22
00:01:33,659 --> 00:01:38,922
Written explanations stay available for human review alongside the structured assessment.

23
00:01:39,322 --> 00:01:45,216
Teachers can review AI feedback and resolve student disputes without erasing the original assessment.

24
00:01:45,216 --> 00:01:48,600
This working prototype still needs a real classroom pilot.
